1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:12,880
Nice kick I told you open your body when you kill the ball

3
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,840
How many times do I have to break it down before you get it?

4
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:22,320
I'm getting tired of explaining to you over and over again

5
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,840
You've got to be the densest person I've ever met you brainless saggy-haired moron

6
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:31,240
If you were in my gang, I'd tie you to my bike and drag your sorry ass all over town

7
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:34,440
Maybe the speed bumps would give your brain the jump start indeed

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,840
What? That's messed up! You can't just threaten people, man. You don't know the first thing about teaching

9
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:17,326
Ugh, I've had enough. Why are you making me kick balls against the wall anyway?

10
00:02:17,646 --> 00:02:21,446
If that's all you wanted me to do, then why are you here? Set it up at least.

11
00:02:21,806 --> 00:02:23,586
Give me a moving target to hit.

12
00:02:24,286 --> 00:02:26,806
Not yet. You're not even close to ready for that.

13
00:02:27,126 --> 00:02:27,566
What?

14
00:02:28,046 --> 00:02:31,926
The first thing on the docket is trying to fix all those bad habits of yours.

15
00:02:32,226 --> 00:02:35,166
But you're not getting it. Problems your head more than anything.

16
00:02:36,126 --> 00:02:37,646
What's that supposed to mean?

17
00:02:38,066 --> 00:02:39,986
See, the goal's not only to kill the ball.

18
00:02:39,986 --> 00:02:43,246
You also gotta think about and be ready for what comes next.

19
00:02:44,786 --> 00:02:46,326
Just kick it at the wall.

20
00:02:48,006 --> 00:02:49,166
Take this!

21
00:02:50,746 --> 00:02:52,566
Quick, pass it straight back to me.

22
00:02:55,846 --> 00:02:57,826
That was way too slow.

23
00:02:58,346 --> 00:03:00,126
Killing the ball's not the end of it.

24
00:03:00,626 --> 00:03:02,906
It's supposed to set you up for what comes next.

25
00:03:03,126 --> 00:03:04,866
That's why it's done in the first place.

26
00:03:05,106 --> 00:03:07,246
You're killing it for funsies!

27
00:03:07,246 --> 00:03:10,626
Is that finally starting to get through that thick skull of your ass?

28
00:03:12,006 --> 00:03:14,326
It's like I'm talking to a brick wall over here.

29
00:03:14,426 --> 00:03:15,666
Why are you not getting it?

30
00:03:15,746 --> 00:03:18,206
You gotta open your body, you hear me?

31
00:03:18,466 --> 00:03:20,346
What do you mean, open my body?

32
00:03:20,506 --> 00:03:23,606
You keep repeating the same thing, but it doesn't make any damn sense.

33
00:03:23,606 --> 00:03:28,326
I guess you're right.

34
00:03:28,646 --> 00:03:29,686
Kind of vague, huh?

35
00:03:31,746 --> 00:03:33,886
Since explaining it to me doesn't work,

36
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:36,566
why don't you show me instead?

37
00:03:39,046 --> 00:03:39,766
How's that?

38
00:03:39,946 --> 00:03:42,646
I bet you can't kill a ball that's coming at you out of nowhere.

39
00:03:42,646 --> 00:03:52,606
That touch was perfect.

40
00:03:53,006 --> 00:03:54,306
Pure poetry in motion.

41
00:03:54,866 --> 00:03:56,106
And that's not the only thing.

42
00:03:56,506 --> 00:03:58,386
He kicked the ball with such precision.

43
00:03:59,546 --> 00:04:01,046
That was lightning fast.

44
00:04:01,206 --> 00:04:03,406
He received the ball and kicked it in the same movement.

45
00:04:03,406 --> 00:04:08,686
Wait, I think I get it.

46
00:04:09,246 --> 00:04:09,626
Huh?

47
00:04:10,426 --> 00:04:11,486
What you did.

48
00:04:11,806 --> 00:04:13,586
The way you killed the ball there.

49
00:04:14,406 --> 00:04:15,466
I see.

50
00:04:16,126 --> 00:04:18,406
So by open, what you mean is...

51
00:04:19,706 --> 00:04:25,006
Oh, sorry.

52
00:04:25,506 --> 00:04:27,546
I wasn't laughing at you or nothing, Ashito.

53
00:04:27,546 --> 00:04:30,526
Yeah, you just made me remember something.

54
00:04:31,906 --> 00:04:33,186
Back in fifth grade,

55
00:04:33,466 --> 00:04:35,986
I went to the National Center for the first time.

56
00:04:36,386 --> 00:04:39,226
The thing is, everyone there knew about me and my upbringing,

57
00:04:39,766 --> 00:04:42,366
which meant that no one paid any attention to me.

58
00:04:42,746 --> 00:04:45,126
In fact, it seemed like they were trying to avoid me.

59
00:04:45,546 --> 00:04:47,786
So I was feeling low when I first met him.

60
00:04:47,906 --> 00:04:48,086
Hey.

61
00:04:50,046 --> 00:04:52,006
You got some real talent there, kid.

62
00:04:53,406 --> 00:04:53,686
Oh.

63
00:04:53,686 --> 00:04:57,646
And for the next 15 minutes,

64
00:04:58,026 --> 00:05:00,666
this guy watched me practice and gave me advice.

65
00:05:01,486 --> 00:05:03,806
He was one of the best teachers I'd ever met.

66
00:05:04,206 --> 00:05:06,026
He knew the exact right way to word things

67
00:05:06,026 --> 00:05:08,706
so they'd stick in my slow, stupid brain.

68
00:05:09,866 --> 00:05:11,026
Thing is...

69
00:05:11,026 --> 00:05:12,746
Quit being stingy, old man.

70
00:05:13,106 --> 00:05:14,526
I don't have all day to waste.

71
00:05:14,686 --> 00:05:16,786
Can't you just tell me what I gotta do to get better?

72
00:05:17,966 --> 00:05:19,546
He had a certain style.

73
00:05:19,906 --> 00:05:22,046
He'd always stop right before he got to the point

74
00:05:22,046 --> 00:05:23,566
where he was spelling it out for me.

75
00:05:23,686 --> 00:05:25,466
I'm not gonna hand you everything.

76
00:05:25,966 --> 00:05:28,186
You're gonna have to find out the answers by yourself.

77
00:05:30,106 --> 00:05:32,026
If you figure it out on your own,

78
00:05:32,566 --> 00:05:34,006
you'll never forget it.

79
00:05:35,206 --> 00:05:36,406
It was Fukuda,

80
00:05:36,886 --> 00:05:39,386
manager of the Asperion Junior Youth Team.

81
00:05:39,586 --> 00:05:40,906
That was his title back then.

82
00:05:41,606 --> 00:05:42,046
Oh.

83
00:05:42,646 --> 00:05:43,646
After that day,

84
00:05:44,166 --> 00:05:47,266
I took the advice he gave me during that 15-minute session

85
00:05:47,266 --> 00:05:49,626
and ended up filling in the blanks

86
00:05:49,626 --> 00:05:51,226
of what he was trying to teach me.

87
00:05:51,526 --> 00:05:54,106
Then practiced it over and over again.

88
00:05:54,106 --> 00:05:57,546
The old man coached you.

89
00:05:59,326 --> 00:05:59,906
Well, well.

90
00:06:00,286 --> 00:06:02,266
I guess he gives good advice when he wants to.

91
00:06:03,266 --> 00:06:03,726
Hey!

92
00:06:03,726 --> 00:06:09,746
I had a feeling you'd be out here training.

93
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,206
Hate to break it to you,

94
00:06:13,326 --> 00:06:14,366
but you suck at lying.

95
00:06:14,706 --> 00:06:16,526
Thought you could sneak off without us, huh?

96
00:06:16,686 --> 00:06:18,926
No way I'm gonna let you beat me that easily.

97
00:06:19,746 --> 00:06:21,606
A couple of busybodies.

98
00:06:23,786 --> 00:06:25,906
If you can figure it out on your own,

99
00:06:27,126 --> 00:06:28,486
you'll never forget it.

100
00:06:28,486 --> 00:06:33,286
We'll round off this week's drills

101
00:06:33,286 --> 00:06:34,406
with something different.

102
00:06:34,826 --> 00:06:37,026
You'll be playing a four-on-four minigame today.

103
00:06:37,766 --> 00:06:38,086
But,

104
00:06:38,486 --> 00:06:40,866
teams will play in a diamond formation.

105
00:06:42,246 --> 00:06:42,926
In this game,

106
00:06:42,986 --> 00:06:44,766
you're only allowed to dribble upfield.

107
00:06:45,106 --> 00:06:45,426
Also,

108
00:06:45,786 --> 00:06:47,786
you're prohibited from taking any long shots

109
00:06:47,786 --> 00:06:48,966
or one-on-one challenges.

110
00:06:49,666 --> 00:06:50,446
In other words,

111
00:06:50,746 --> 00:06:52,846
you and your team must pass your way to the goal.

112
00:06:53,546 --> 00:06:55,226
If you can't kill and kick the ball,

113
00:06:55,786 --> 00:06:57,826
you won't be able to take part in this game.

114
00:06:57,826 --> 00:06:59,126
In which case,

115
00:06:59,526 --> 00:07:00,946
you'll have to leave the field.

116
00:07:03,666 --> 00:07:04,966
You gonna be okay?

117
00:07:07,166 --> 00:07:07,886
Tyra.

118
00:07:10,046 --> 00:07:12,446
Just keep passing the ball to me.

119
00:07:12,906 --> 00:07:14,406
There's no need to go easy.

120
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,006
All right, let's go.

121
00:07:22,186 --> 00:07:24,066
Your body's way too stiff.

122
00:07:24,126 --> 00:07:25,146
You gotta loosen up.

123
00:07:26,986 --> 00:07:27,426
Nice.

124
00:07:27,426 --> 00:07:28,306
Pass it back.

125
00:07:31,346 --> 00:07:33,046
All I gotta do is relax.

126
00:07:34,446 --> 00:07:35,886
Even though it's a minigame,

127
00:07:35,946 --> 00:07:36,886
it's still a game,

128
00:07:36,966 --> 00:07:38,766
which means I can have all the fun I want.

129
00:07:38,766 --> 00:07:43,106
Aoi's their weakest link.

130
00:07:43,186 --> 00:07:44,846
Pressure him and he'll cave in.

131
00:07:46,526 --> 00:07:47,186
Press him!

132
00:07:47,906 --> 00:07:49,806
You keep kicking the ball way too low.

133
00:07:54,146 --> 00:07:55,786
I refuse to give up.

134
00:07:55,786 --> 00:08:00,246
The goal's not only to kill the ball.

135
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:02,106
You gotta be ready for what comes next.

136
00:08:02,246 --> 00:08:02,546
Here.

137
00:08:02,546 --> 00:08:10,006
What I'm trying to do is move the ball.

138
00:08:10,006 --> 00:08:12,226
I have to think about where I want it to go

139
00:08:12,226 --> 00:08:12,846
before I even touch it.

140
00:08:12,846 --> 00:08:13,686
Before I even touch it.

141
00:08:13,686 --> 00:08:16,846
This entire time.

142
00:08:16,846 --> 00:08:20,146
I was so hung up on making sure that I stopped the ball.

143
00:08:20,146 --> 00:08:22,526
All I focused on was keeping it at my feet.

144
00:08:22,526 --> 00:08:23,986
Even when I was being crowded.

145
00:08:24,766 --> 00:08:26,186
Right back at you, Aoi.

146
00:08:26,186 --> 00:08:28,266
But that's not how you do it.

147
00:08:28,266 --> 00:08:28,846
Ah!

148
00:08:29,526 --> 00:08:31,106
You gotta open your body.

149
00:08:31,226 --> 00:08:32,026
You hear me?

150
00:08:32,026 --> 00:08:35,206
I open my body to widen my field of view.

151
00:08:35,406 --> 00:08:38,106
That way I can position myself to pass the ball anywhere.

152
00:08:38,786 --> 00:08:40,106
Since I'm right-footed,

153
00:08:40,106 --> 00:08:42,946
I'll kill the ball so it stops diagonally to my right.

154
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,706
Nagano's coming in for the tackle,

155
00:08:47,166 --> 00:08:48,706
but he's still too far away.

156
00:08:49,086 --> 00:08:50,866
It feels like I've got so much more time

157
00:08:50,866 --> 00:08:52,046
to think and move now.

158
00:08:57,826 --> 00:08:59,806
You're finally getting it, Ashito.

159
00:09:00,966 --> 00:09:01,166
Huh?

160
00:09:02,026 --> 00:09:06,066
Every training drill we do has a purpose.

161
00:09:06,066 --> 00:09:09,146
If I understand the reasoning behind each drill

162
00:09:09,146 --> 00:09:11,446
and focus on improving that aspect,

163
00:09:11,746 --> 00:09:12,746
I'll get even better.

164
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:16,066
I really owe you guys Tachibana,

165
00:09:16,326 --> 00:09:17,906
Otomo, and Togashi.

166
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:18,506
Here!

167
00:09:18,966 --> 00:09:19,546
Nice!

168
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:22,126
Our strategy isn't working out.

169
00:09:22,466 --> 00:09:23,046
Change it up.

170
00:09:23,386 --> 00:09:24,806
Let's block all their passing channels.

171
00:09:25,266 --> 00:09:26,346
So awesome!

172
00:09:26,346 --> 00:09:26,846
Dumball.

173
00:09:32,146 --> 00:09:32,626
Owie!

174
00:09:34,466 --> 00:09:36,186
It never occurred to me

175
00:09:36,186 --> 00:09:38,326
that something as simple as how I stopped the ball

176
00:09:38,326 --> 00:09:39,466
would be so important.

177
00:09:40,306 --> 00:09:42,346
By learning how to do it the right way,

178
00:09:42,506 --> 00:09:44,686
it feels like the scope of my soccer

179
00:09:44,686 --> 00:09:46,146
has broadened.

180
00:09:46,146 --> 00:09:54,266
Get in there!

181
00:09:54,266 --> 00:09:58,766
Oh, crap!

182
00:10:01,266 --> 00:10:02,266
Eat that!

183
00:10:02,266 --> 00:10:02,846
Oh, yeah!

184
00:10:03,406 --> 00:10:04,606
Nice one, Taita!

185
00:10:04,686 --> 00:10:05,646
Great shot!

186
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,506
And of course, nice one, May!

187
00:10:07,686 --> 00:10:08,566
I'm the best!

188
00:10:09,686 --> 00:10:10,246
Pass!

189
00:10:11,526 --> 00:10:12,086
Yeah.

190
00:10:12,466 --> 00:10:13,586
Good stuff, Ashito.

191
00:10:13,586 --> 00:10:20,626
I know you've been helping

192
00:10:20,626 --> 00:10:22,186
with his nighttime training sessions.

193
00:10:22,706 --> 00:10:23,806
He's improved.

194
00:10:23,946 --> 00:10:24,986
Crazy fast, too.

195
00:10:25,826 --> 00:10:26,866
So tell me,

196
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:28,586
what all did you teach him?

197
00:10:29,246 --> 00:10:29,986
Nothing much,

198
00:10:30,086 --> 00:10:31,226
just the normal stuff.

199
00:10:32,066 --> 00:10:32,946
I didn't teach him

200
00:10:32,946 --> 00:10:34,486
about barking instructions.

201
00:10:36,206 --> 00:10:37,186
That guy

202
00:10:37,186 --> 00:10:38,806
has got the eyes.

203
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:40,806
Finally,

204
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:43,086
he's found his way

205
00:10:43,086 --> 00:10:44,106
to the starting line.

206
00:10:45,426 --> 00:10:46,246
Ashito Owie,

207
00:10:46,726 --> 00:10:48,026
I will teach you

208
00:10:48,026 --> 00:10:48,826
how to play soccer.

209
00:11:06,926 --> 00:11:08,066
Manager Shimomura,

210
00:11:08,586 --> 00:11:10,146
thanks for helping us

211
00:11:10,146 --> 00:11:11,506
round out our training session.

212
00:11:11,966 --> 00:11:13,206
It was a good practice game.

213
00:11:13,706 --> 00:11:14,506
I should have never

214
00:11:14,506 --> 00:11:15,726
agreed to this match.

215
00:11:19,386 --> 00:11:20,406
This isn't how

216
00:11:20,406 --> 00:11:21,906
high schoolers play soccer.

217
00:11:22,666 --> 00:11:23,406
They're on a whole

218
00:11:23,406 --> 00:11:24,206
different level.

219
00:11:25,426 --> 00:11:26,646
The number one team

220
00:11:26,646 --> 00:11:28,226
in the U18 Premier League,

221
00:11:28,466 --> 00:11:29,366
the Tokyo City

222
00:11:29,366 --> 00:11:30,766
Asperion Youth Club.

223
00:11:32,646 --> 00:11:33,846
Manager Fukuda,

224
00:11:34,646 --> 00:11:35,846
your players over there,

225
00:11:36,066 --> 00:11:36,766
are they okay?

226
00:11:37,186 --> 00:11:37,926
They seem more

227
00:11:37,926 --> 00:11:39,226
exhausted than the others.

228
00:11:39,226 --> 00:11:40,506
Yeah,

229
00:11:41,046 --> 00:11:42,446
those guys just recently

230
00:11:42,446 --> 00:11:43,426
joined the A-Team.

231
00:11:43,986 --> 00:11:44,886
And, well,

232
00:11:45,226 --> 00:11:46,186
they need a little time

233
00:11:46,186 --> 00:11:46,766
to adjust.

234
00:11:46,966 --> 00:11:48,766
Something doesn't seem right.

235
00:11:49,146 --> 00:11:50,026
Is it really because

236
00:11:50,026 --> 00:11:51,086
they're new to the team?

237
00:11:54,586 --> 00:11:55,886
You look pathetic.

238
00:11:56,426 --> 00:11:57,166
Get on your feet,

239
00:11:57,266 --> 00:11:57,586
newbie.

240
00:11:58,786 --> 00:11:59,286
Akutsu,

241
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:01,166
this is how we do

242
00:12:01,166 --> 00:12:02,126
things around here.

243
00:12:02,366 --> 00:12:03,206
Don't like it?

244
00:12:03,346 --> 00:12:03,706
Leave.

245
00:12:04,466 --> 00:12:05,846
Shape up or ship out.

246
00:12:05,846 --> 00:12:08,166
It's a shame

247
00:12:08,166 --> 00:12:09,586
Kuribayashi isn't here.

248
00:12:10,086 --> 00:12:10,806
We could have scored

249
00:12:10,806 --> 00:12:12,006
four more goals.

250
00:12:12,226 --> 00:12:13,166
You better not be

251
00:12:13,166 --> 00:12:14,166
blaming us for that.

252
00:12:14,206 --> 00:12:15,046
Of course not.

253
00:12:15,406 --> 00:12:16,406
That isn't what I meant.

254
00:12:17,146 --> 00:12:18,206
What I'm saying is,

255
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,566
this isn't even close

256
00:12:19,566 --> 00:12:20,446
to the soccer manager

257
00:12:20,446 --> 00:12:21,546
Fukuda had in mind.

258
00:12:23,746 --> 00:12:24,426
Can it!

259
00:12:24,506 --> 00:12:25,086
All of you!

260
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,206
Save it for later!

261
00:12:27,066 --> 00:12:28,006
Do us a favor

262
00:12:28,006 --> 00:12:28,886
and quit bringing up

263
00:12:28,886 --> 00:12:29,826
people who aren't here.

264
00:12:30,146 --> 00:12:30,986
We're the only members

265
00:12:30,986 --> 00:12:32,066
of the A-Team now.

266
00:12:32,066 --> 00:12:34,026
Seriously?

267
00:12:34,446 --> 00:12:35,746
We got nine goals

268
00:12:35,746 --> 00:12:36,366
and they're arguing

269
00:12:36,366 --> 00:12:37,106
about how we could

270
00:12:37,106 --> 00:12:37,806
have scored more?

271
00:12:38,226 --> 00:12:39,246
I never imagined

272
00:12:39,246 --> 00:12:39,886
that the A-Team

273
00:12:39,886 --> 00:12:40,766
would be this good.

274
00:12:41,806 --> 00:12:42,786
The soccer that I've

275
00:12:42,786 --> 00:12:43,726
known up to this point

276
00:12:43,726 --> 00:12:45,346
is nothing compared

277
00:12:45,346 --> 00:12:45,926
to the soccer

278
00:12:45,926 --> 00:12:46,826
these guys play.

279
00:12:50,106 --> 00:12:51,306
